   "body": "Pushed a follow-up commit (62ab031): `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` from the environment is now only used when the access key and secret also come from the environment. If explicit keys are passed in `api_config`, a leftover environment token is no longer attached to them (that mix would fail authentication). Added a unit test for this case.\n\nThis comment was drafted with Claude Code.\n"
